  "basis": "The chart title explicitly defines the metric as 'Price in U.S. dollars per barrel', overriding the mislabeled y-axis 'Count'. The vertical axis increases from 0 at the top to 35 at the bottom, meaning higher values are plotted lower. The data point for 1980 is the lowest on the chart, indicating the lowest price. The highest price is at 1976 (approximately 17) and 1977 (approximately 16). Therefore, the year with the highest per-barrel cost is 1976. The option 'Route 1976 escalation review' is the correct choice.",
